coastline_south_40s.geojson
---------------------------

Natural Earth 1:50m coastline (ne_50m_coastline), clipped to
south of 40 degrees S. 170 LineString features, EPSG:4326 (OGC:CRS84
longitude, latitude order), coordinates rounded to 4 decimal places. One
attribute, featurecla.

Source: https://www.naturalearthdata.com/, file
geojson/ne_50m_coastline.geojson from
https://github.com/nvkelso/natural-earth-vector (master branch, downloaded
2026-09-30).

License: public domain. Natural Earth data are in the public domain; see
https://www.naturalearthdata.com/about/terms-of-use/.

Made with GDAL (via gdalraster::ogr2ogr) using:

  ogr2ogr -f GeoJSON -nln coastline_south_40s \
    -clipsrc -180 -90 180 -40 \
    -explodecollections -nlt LINESTRING -select featurecla \
    -lco COORDINATE_PRECISION=4 -lco RFC7946=NO -lco WRITE_BBOX=NO \
    coastline_south_40s.geojson ne_50m_coastline.geojson

polar_3031.tif, polar_lonlat.tif
--------------------------------

Synthetic SST-like field (degrees C) as Cloud Optimized GeoTIFFs, made by
tools/make-polar-cogs.R with GDAL's COG driver: Int16 with scale 0.001 and
nodata -32768, 128 x 128 tiles, 3 overviews. Cells north of 40S and on a
lobed "land" ring (not real land) are nodata; data resume south of 85S.
Six 60-degree sectors, a ring at 60S and a blob on the antimeridian at 55S
make rotation, mirroring and seams visible.

  polar_3031.tif    EPSG:3031, 400 x 400 cells of 32 km over +-6400 km,
                    DEFLATE, horizontal predictor.
  polar_lonlat.tif  EPSG:4326, 720 x 100 cells of 0.5 degrees, lon -180..180,
                    lat -40..-90, LZW, horizontal predictor. Covers the pole;
                    the antimeridian is at its edges.

License: generated data, same license as the package.

polar_rgba.tif, polar_ycbcr.tif
-------------------------------

Synthetic colour images as Cloud Optimized GeoTIFFs, made by
tools/make-rgb-cogs.R with GDAL's COG driver: EPSG:3031, 250 x 250 cells of
32 km over +-4000 km, 128 x 128 tiles, 2 overviews.

  polar_rgba.tif    4-band Byte RGBA (Red, Green, Blue, Alpha), LZW, pixel
                    interleaved. Flat quadrants: red towards 0 (up), green
                    towards 90E (right), blue towards 180 (down), yellow
                    towards 90W (left), white rings every 1000 km. Alpha 0
                    beyond 3800 km, 128 from 2400 to 2600 km, else 255.
  polar_ycbcr.tif   3-band Byte RGB stored as YCbCr JPEG (photometric 6,
                    quality 85), with shared JPEGTables per image. A colour
                    wheel: hue by angle clockwise from 0 (red at 0, green at
                    120E, blue at 120W), white at the pole, dark rings every
                    1000 km.

License: generated data, same license as the package.

probe/*.arrows
--------------

The polar probe's data (probe_scene()): byte copies of the six blobs in
allboa/design origin/2026-09-30/probe/bundle.json, written by that
record's prep.py with pyarrow from Natural Earth 50m land and coastline
(public domain), a graticule with an RGBA colour column, and a synthetic
SST-like field with its pre-projected mesh. Interleaved GeoArrow in
EPSG:3031 (PROJJSON). land, coast and graticule carry no attribute
columns besides the graticule's colour, so a popup on them has nothing to
show.
